# `npm run lint` already gives prettier an explicit list of what it formats —
# this project's TypeScript and its JSON — so this file is the backstop for
# editor integrations that run prettier over whatever is open.
#
# The boundary is ownership, not strictness. Markdown belongs to markdownlint
# (.markdownlint.yaml, `make lint-docs`); mkdocs.yml and docs/ belong to the docs
# toolchain; .github/workflows/ is YAML that actionlint and CodeQL read. A second
# formatter with its own opinion about those files does not make the project
# tidier, it makes `make lint` fail on a fresh scaffold.
*.md
mkdocs.yml
docs/
site/
.github/

# Generated, vendored, or produced by a build.
dist/
coverage/
node_modules/
package-lock.json
*.min.js
